# E §10 readers-of (tally 2.1.7 B2, issue #133; P64): a move whose day reads d2 and whose amount reads it too is
# one reader, pay2. 2.1.6's refcore printed `pay2, pay2`. (T's G11 r_p_c2.)
=== r_p_c2.tally
model pc
  tally 2
  on 2026-12-31
  start 2026-01-01
  end 2026-12-31

source card "card"

unit PLN: currency minor 0.01

input amt: money PLN

input d2: date

input d0: date

place konto: accounts PLN lives 2026-01-01..

place world: outside lives 1900-01-01..

move pay2: transfers
  on d2
  leg cash from konto to world amount if d2 > d0 then amt else amt

ask r_d2: readers-of d2
ask r_amt: readers-of amt
ask r_d0: readers-of d0
ask v: bal(konto, 2026-12-31)

version card_2026
  cite card
  governs always
  known 2026-01-01
  amt = 1.00 PLN
  d2 = 2026-05-01
  d0 = 2026-01-01
  opening[konto] = 500.00 PLN at 2026-01-01 start
=== expect r_d2 r_d0 r_amt
r_d2: pay2
r_d0: pay2
r_amt: pay2
